SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Apostoloi\, Antimachia
LOCATION:Antimachia\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Antimachia\, the big windmill village in the middle of the island\, has its patronal feast for the Holy Apostles on 29-30 June\, with vespers and a glendi with local music and food on the square. The same village feasts the Panagia on 15 August and runs the honey festival in August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#antimachia-panigiri-of-agioi-apostoloi-antimachia
